.TH ROLLING_HELPER 8 "2026-11-20" "rolling-linux 2.1.11" "Rolling WWAN Services Manual"
.SH NAME
rolling_helper \- D\-Bus helper service for the Rolling Linux apps
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /usr/bin/rolling_helper
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rolling_helper
provides the
.B com.rolling.helper
D\-Bus API used by the Rolling
.BR rolling_config (8),
.BR rolling_flash (8)
and
.BR rolling_ma (8)
services.  It is started by
.BR systemd (1)
as
.B rolling_helper.service
and runs as a system daemon; it is not normally started by hand.
.PP
The universal package ships one helper binary per OEM under
.I /usr/lib/rolling/rolling_helper_service/helper_set/
(one subdirectory per project and OEM).
The installed
.B /usr/bin/rolling_helper
is a small dispatcher: it reads the machine vendor from the DMI tables
.RI ( /sys/class/dmi/id/sys_vendor ,
falling back to
.IR /sys/class/dmi/id/board_vendor )
and execs the matching OEM variant, so the same package serves every
OEM.  On an unknown vendor it prints an error and exits non\-zero
instead of running a wrong\-OEM helper; the failure is visible in the
service journal.
.SH OPTIONS
.B rolling_helper
takes no command\-line options; it is managed through systemd.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/rolling/rolling_helper_service/helper_set/
Per\-OEM helper binaries; each
.B <project>_<oem>
subdirectory contains that OEM's
.B rolling_helper
executable.
.TP
.I /usr/share/dbus\-1/system.d/com.rolling.helper.conf
D\-Bus system bus policy for the
.B com.rolling.helper
name.
.SH SYSTEMD
.B rolling_helper.service
is ordered after
.BR ModemManager.service .
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
systemctl daemon\-reload
systemctl enable rolling_helper.service
systemctl start rolling_helper.service
systemctl status rolling_helper.service
.fi
.PP
Watch the service journal:
.nf
journalctl \-u rolling_helper.service
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rolling_config (8),
.BR rolling_flash (8),
.BR rolling_ma (8),
.BR ModemManager (8),
.BR systemd (1)
